TLDR by [~accountid:5ab52e9233719f2a50171d43]: 

{quote}As SRE Dat team, we have been maintaining the main key value DB in Bolt - Redis.  In this epic, we had some plans to research and test different technologies for key-value storage. We had two things in mind - to have better durability, and also better [scalability.At|http://scalability.At] that time we had only master-slave architecture for Redises, and we could not scale an instance to bigger from 1 CPU or 64 GB of RAM.Eventually, we found that we didn't have enough resources in the team to take in new technologies and databases. It takes considerable effort, know-how, and time investment to run stateful things at Bolt scale. So we kept to our roots with Redis and started using [Redis-cluster|https://redis.io/docs/management/scaling/], which solved the Redis scalability problem and also improved reliability.{quote}

